course: dictionary
lesson: 6559
title: Nice, and what it really means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Nice» is one of the most common words in English, and it can mean different things. The words around it are your clues. Ask yourself what the sentence is about, and whether the situation sounds good or bad.
explain: «We had a nice day at the beach.» Here nice means pleasant and enjoyable. «She is nice to everyone» means she is kind and friendly. It is the same word with two meanings, and the context tells you which one.
explain: Sometimes «nice» is not praise at all. If your friend drops the cake and you say «Nice one!» in a flat, mocking voice, you mean the opposite. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence, and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Nice is an adjective. Its forms are nice, nicer and nicest.
fact: «Nice» means pleasant, enjoyable or good, as in «a nice day».
fact: «Nice» can mean kind and friendly, as in «She is nice to everyone».
fact: «Nice» can be sarcastic, meaning the opposite of praise, as in «Nice one!» after a mistake.
fact: A stranger who seems nice may still be unsafe. Being nice does not mean you have to do what they say; tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «We had a nice day at the beach.» What does nice mean here? | Very quiet | Sharp and dangerous | *Pleasant and enjoyable | Nasty and cold
exercise: Mia's friend drops the cake, and Mia says «Nice one!» in a flat, mocking voice. What does she mean? | She is asking for a slice | *She is mocking the mistake, the opposite of praise | She is praising a perfect cake | She is saying the cake is very quiet
exercise: «She is nice to everyone.» What does nice mean? | *Kind and friendly | Good-looking | Pleasant weather | Short and rude
test: «The bath water was nice and warm.» What does nice and warm mean? | Very cold and wet | *Pleasantly warm | Boiling and dangerous | Warm, but only for a minute
test: A friend says a new boy «has a nice personality» in a sly way. What might she mean? | That he is the best-looking boy in school | That he is always kind to animals | *That he is not very good-looking | That he is a natural leader
exam: A stranger says, «You seem nice, come with me.» What is the safest answer? | Give them your address to be polite | *Say no, and tell a trusted adult straight away | Go with them, because nice people are always safe | Keep it secret and go with them quietly
